IO-36: resolve a relative RDII interface file name against the input file's folder

iface_readFileParams() passes every [FILES] name through addAbsolutePath(),
which prefixes a relative name with the input file's folder, except the RDII
file name. USE RDII therefore looked for the file in the working directory
(ERROR 343 when the engine is not started from the project folder) and SAVE
RDII wrote it there, while SAVE OUTFLOWS on the next line went next to the
.inp. The RDII name now goes through addAbsolutePath() like the others.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-36_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/iface.c b/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
index 23272de..c95c646 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/iface.c
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ int iface_readFileParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
 
       case RDII_FILE:
         Frdii.mode = k;
-        sstrncpy(Frdii.name, fname, MAXFNAME);
+        sstrncpy(Frdii.name, addAbsolutePath(fname), MAXFNAME);
         break;
 
       case INFLOWS_FILE:
